# Line-ending normalization for build-critical files.
#
# SQLite migration files are embedded into the Rust binary at compile time via
# include_str! and their SHA-384 checksums are stored in _sqlx_migrations. If the
# working-tree line endings of these files differ between checkouts/builds (which
# happens under core.autocrlf=true with no attributes), each release can embed
# different bytes for the same migration version. The installed DB then holds a
# checksum that no longer matches the embedded bytes, and tauri-plugin-sql's sqlx
# migrator panics with MigrateError::VersionMismatch at plugin init — before any
# window is created, producing a silent no-launch on update.
#
# Forcing LF guarantees include_str! embeds identical bytes on every machine and
# every build, permanently stopping per-release checksum drift.

# All SQL files (migrations + any other embedded SQL) — normalize to LF.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders: pin the migrations directory explicitly regardless of
# extension, so any future non-.sql migration asset is covered too.
src-tauri/migrations/** text eol=lf
